{
 "text": "Today we want to solve this system: two x plus y equals three, and x minus two y equals minus one. We'll look at it two ways, the row picture and the column picture, and they give the same answer. In the row picture each equation is a line in the plane and the solution is the point where those two lines cross each other. From the second equation, x equals two y minus one. Can we also eliminate x first? Yes, elimination works either way. Does the order matter? No, you get the same solution.",
